   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the financial services law, in relation to requiring private\nnonprofit postsecondary providers of higher education which service student\nloans to submit an annual report relating to student loan services provided",
    "basePrintNo": "S7752",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7752-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §711, Bank L",
    "lawSection": "Financial Services Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7752\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the financial services law, in relation to requiring\nprivate nonprofit postsecondary providers of higher education which\nservice student loans to submit an annual report relating to student\nloan services provided\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRequires private nonprofit postsecondary providers of higher education\nthat service their own student loans to comply with the reporting\nrequirements applicable to licensed student loan servicers.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1:Requires private nonprofit postsecondary providers of higher\neducation to submit an annual report, due on April 1, to the Department\nof Financial Services containing information on private education debt\nthey service.\n\nSection 2: Effective Date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 627 of the Laws of 2024 requires licensed student loan servicers\nto report information on private education debt they service. However,\nprivate nonprofit postsecondary providers of higher education that\nservice student loans are exempt from Article 14-a of the Banking Law\nand are therefore not subject to this reporting requirement. This bill\nseeks to close that loophole. To promote greater transparency in the\nstudent loan market-including, but not limited to, trends in loan origi-\nnation, terms and conditions, differences in financing costs across\ndemographic groups, and default rates-this bill would require private\nnonprofit postsecondary providers of higher education to report informa-\ntion on private education debt they service, as directed by the super-\nintendent.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
